"[2603.07300] AutoResearch-RL: Perpetual Self-Evaluating Reinforcement Learning Agents for Autonomous Neural Architecture Discovery (https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07300)\nciteturn32216view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07300\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 166\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: This paper has been withdrawn by arXiv Admin\nL9: \nL10: [Submitted on 7 Mar 2026 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 19 Mar 2026 (this version, v2)]\nL11: # Title:AutoResearch-RL: Perpetual Self-Evaluating Reinforcement Learning Agents for Autonomous Neural Architecture Discovery\nL12: \nL13: Authors:cite6†Nilesh Jain , cite7†Rohit Yadav , cite8†Sagar Kotian , cite9†Claude AI L14: \nL15: View a PDF of the paper titled AutoResearch-RL: Perpetual Self-Evaluating Reinforcement Learning Agents for Autonomous Neural Architecture Discovery, by Nilesh Jain and 3 other authors\nL16: \nL17: cite10†No PDF available, click to view other formats L18: > Abstract:We present AutoResearch-RL, a framework in which a reinforcement learning agent conducts open-ended neural architecture and hyperparameter research without human supervision, running perpetually until a termination oracle signals convergence or resource exhaustion.\nL19: At each step the agent proposes a code modification to a target training script, executes it under a fixed wall clock time budget, observes a scalar reward derived from validation bits-per-byte (val-bpb), and updates its policy via Proximal Policy Optimisation (PPO).\nL20: > The key design insight is the separation of three concerns: (i) a frozen environment (data pipeline, evaluation protocol, and constants) that guarantees fair cross-experiment comparison; (ii) a mutable target file (cite11†this http URL†train.py ) that represents the agent's editable state; and (iii) a meta-learner (the RL agent itself) that accumulates a growing trajectory of experiment outcomes and uses them to inform subsequent proposals.\nL21: > We formalise this as a Markov Decision Process, derive convergence guarantees under mild assumptions, and demonstrate empirically on a single GPU nanochat pretraining benchmark that AutoResearch-RL discovers configurations that match or exceed hand-tuned baselines after approximately 300 overnight iterations, with no human in the loop.\nL22: Comments:  | arXiv admin note: This submission has been withdrawn due to violation of arXiv policies for acceptable submissions\nL23: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL24: Cite as:  | cite12†arXiv:2603.07300 [cs.LG]\nL25:    | (or cite13†arXiv:2603.07300v2 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL26:    | cite14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2603.07300†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL27: ## Submission history\nL28: \nL29: From: arXiv Admin [cite15†view email ]\nL30: cite5†[v1] Sat, 7 Mar 2026 17:49:44 UTC (14 KB)\nL31: [v2] Thu, 19 Mar 2026 13:59:07 UTC (1 KB) (withdrawn)\nL32: \nL33: Full-text links:\nL34: \nL35: ## Access Paper:\nL36: \nL37: View a PDF of the paper titled AutoResearch-RL: Perpetual Self-Evaluating Reinforcement Learning Agents for Autonomous Neural Architecture Discovery, by Nilesh Jain and 3 other authors\nL38: \nL39:   * Withdrawn\nL40: \nL41: No license for this version due to withdrawn\nL42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.LG\nL45: \nL46: cite16†< prev |   cite17†next > L47: \nL48: cite18†new | cite19†recent | cite20†2026-03 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite21†cs L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite22†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite24†Sema